Description:

Oops! Someone accidentally sent an important file to a network printer—can you retrieve it from the print server?
The printer is on 59308. You can try $ nc -vz mysterious-sea.picoctf.net 59308
Hints:
1. knowing how SMB protocol works would be helpful!
2. smbclient and smbutil are good tools

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

As the hint suggests us to run smbclient we check for the List available shares on servers with anonymous access
using cmd "smbclient -L //mysterious-sea.picoctf.net -p 59308 -N" this showed us the list that containted Shares
and IPC we then connect to Shares using "smbclient //mysterious-sea.picoctf.net/shares -p 59308 -N" which opens 
us a cmd line here we type "get flag.txt" to get the flag then exit to the main webshell and cat flag.txt to 
get the ctf's flag.

